      "rationale": "Confirmed intrauterine first-trimester pregnancy (~9-10 weeks) with near-daily use of two opioids (hydrocodone/acetaminophen and tramadol) for chronic pain — a prolonged exposure that carries boxed-warning risk of neonatal opioid withdrawal syndrome and requires a coordinated, gradual taper now, not later.",
      "draftedAction": "Contact the patient's pain specialist this week to co-develop a written, gradual opioid taper schedule; give the patient the written schedule, as she responds well to concrete plans. Counsel explicitly to continue current lowest-effective dosing until the taper begins and NOT to stop opioids abruptly, given maternal and fetal withdrawal risk. Start pregnancy-safe nonpharmacologic pain management (physical therapy referral, heat, stretching, activity pacing) and reassess pain control and taper progress at every prenatal visit. Document opioid exposure for delivery planning so the newborn is assessed for neonatal opioid withdrawal syndrome.",
